      "topic": "staff",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "title": {
        "en": "Dedicated doctors and empathetic veterinary technicians"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Clients praise Dr. Green, Dr. DiPolo, Dr. Boulting, and Dr. Stern for combining thorough medical expertise with genuine empathy for anxious pets and owners. Multiple reviewers mention that veterinarians take unhurried time to review treatment choices. A few reviewers noted feelings of reduced personal connection over time or frustration during isolated visits."
      },
      "mentions": 19
    },
    {
      "topic": "communication",
      "sentiment": "positive",
      "title": {
        "en": "Responsive messaging and thorough explanations"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Pet parents highlight excellent communication through email and text help lines, noting that clinical staff answer pre-visit questions promptly. Veterinarians receive praise for walking through complex treatment paths in plain terms. One client, however, experienced frustration trying to obtain diagnostic lab results when a treating doctor worked on a part-time schedule."
      },
      "mentions": 9
    },
    {
      "topic": "animals",
      "sentiment": "mixed",
      "title": {
        "en": "Gentle handling despite past trauma complaint"
      },
      "text": {
        "en": "Many reviewers emphasize that veterinarians and assistants are sensitive to stressed or squirmy pets, handling rescue dogs and short-nosed breeds with great patience and affectionate care. Pet parents feel their animals are kept comfortable during examinations and surgery. However, one historical review noted an extremely traumatic spaying experience that left a cat fearful of strangers."
      },
      "mentions": 4
    }
  ],
